From d6806a94a28ebe9a344ba4478e71190717236ff3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:05:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] respawn guard: a park that names its PR covers its
 run's own note first naming it

The respawn guard held the CI wake of a card that followed ship's request-review
flow, because the parking run's own summary note was the card's first comment
naming the PR the park itself awaited.

restated_after_park now also counts as known the PRs the latest orderly park
event names itself: awaiting.ref when it is a bare PR URL, PR URLs in its reason,
and `--repo O/R --number N` in its wake_check (ship's --review-ci-probe). The
existing proofs stay: one commented event per row, written by the parking run
(portable writer_run_uid on synced schemas), at/after the park and before the
next claim. Another run's note, or a note naming a PR neither the earlier
comments nor the park name, keeps the hold.

Five whys (2026-11-13, MacBook t_01a1cff0541bf30c, PR #2208)
- Why 1: active_pr_reason saw PR comment 10914 (04:26:25 PST) newer than the
  latest orderly park (04:26:18), so the park was not a handoff:
  respawn_guarded {"reason": "active_pr"} at 04:37:19, after condition_met
  04:37:13; operator `kanban resume` at 04:41:18.
- Why 2: restated_after_park counts the parking run's own note only when every
  PR it names was named in the card's comments before the park; #2208 was first
  named in that note.
- Why 3: the park itself names #2208 (awaiting.ref and the review-ci-probe
  wake_check), but `known` ignored the park event's own payload. Ship's
  request-review flow always produces this order: open the PR, park on its CI,
  post the summary.
- Root (happened): 74b9347149 (11-12, same card, PR #1486) recognized only
  restatements of PRs named before the park.
- Root (not caught): its tests covered restated PRs and the new-PR refusal, none
  the event shape ship's own request-review action produces.

Proof
- New tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_pr_park_names_pr.py (27 cases):
  T1 claimed -> scheduled/continued park with awaiting.ref = PR and the
  review-ci-probe wake_check -> same run's note first naming the PR ->
  condition_met: active_pr_reason None and check_respawn_guard None (synced and
  local schemas; each park field alone also suffices). T2 the note also names a
  PR the park does not name: held. T3 the note is another run's: held.
  park_named_prs field-parsing table.
- RED on main's logic: dropping the new `known |=` line fails 7 (T1 cases).
  12 mutants of park_named_prs / the hook, each killed.
- T4: every test file importing active_pr_reason, kanban_pr_park_note,
  kanban_pr_same_run_park or kanban_db_dispatch_pr_state passes unchanged.
- Incident replay: a copy of worker-3's Board replica (sync-shadow/default.db)
  cut back to t_01a1cff0541bf30c's 04:37:19 respawn_guarded tick (events kept:
  scheduled 767388, commented 767393 = comment 10914, condition_met 769092):
  main -> active_pr / active_pr; branch -> None / None.
- Real-row replay (guard allows more): restated_after_park main vs branch over
  every card with an orderly park and PR comments on worker-3's replicas of the
  default, bb and askeve boards plus its local board: 0 of 1245 change at their
  current state.
